poken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mend ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to repair, especially with cloth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Here and there, the clothing requires mending or cleaning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about a cultural festival.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "leopard skin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the hide of a wild cat with spots", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The women's traditional leopard skin clothing needs to be brought out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "full moon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when the moon is seen as a full disc ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Also because the full moon hasn't arrived up to now. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "affair", "type": "name"}, {"content": "matter; issue", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The men stay in the villages, to relax and focus on land affairs that require discussing. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stick", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a longish slim piece of wood ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The women bring sticks, which symbolize spears that need to be thrown at the men. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mock battle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a play fight", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After that, there are other games, dancing, and mock battles that need to be enjoyed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to symbolize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stand for another thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The sticks, which symbolize spears. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chief", "type": "name"}, {"content": "head of the village", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, people move to the chief's palace for speeches and praise songs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to display", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On Sunday, the best cattle from each family are to displayed to impress the neighbors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le05ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Gerunds and Infinitives with Need, Require and Want", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use different rules for infinitives and gerunds when they come after the verbs <span class=\"italic\">need</span>, <span class=\"italic\">want</span> and <span class=\"italic\">require</span>.<br/>  The rule depends on whether you want a passive or active meaning.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The verbs <span class=\"italic\">need</span>, <span class=\"italic\">want</span> and <span class=\"italic\">require</span> can be followed by an active or passive infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">need to give him</span> a quick call. (active meaning) <br/> Sometimes, people <span class=\"strong\">don't need to be told</span> the truth. (passive meaning) </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">My position <span class=\"strong\">requires me to accommodate</span> many different personalities. (active meaning) <br/> They <span class=\"strong\">required the project to be delivered </span>by the end of the day. (passive meaning) </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">wanted to stay</span> a little while longer. (active meaning) <br/> It was obvious that <span class=\"strong\">he wanted to be included</span>. (passive meaning)</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Active gerunds, however, after these verbs express passive meanings:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Your beard <span class=\"strong\">needs shaving</span>.</span> (It should be shaved.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">These documents <span class=\"strong\">require</span> careful <span class=\"strong\">handling</span>.</span> (They should be handled carefully.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The tables <span class=\"strong\">want cleaning</span>.</span> (They should be cleaned.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The women's traditional leopard skin clothing <span class=\"strong\">needs to be</span> brought out. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It <span class=\"strong\">needs to be</span> carefully looked at. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Every woman <span class=\"strong\">wants to be told</span> that her garment is beautiful. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Both of these are <span class=\"strong\">required to happen</span> before the ceremony can begin.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are spears that <span class=\"strong\">need to be</span> thrown at the men. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Appreciation gifts are <span class=\"strong\">required to be given to</span> performers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "After that, there are other games, dancing, and mock battles that <span class=\"strong\">need to be</span> enjoyed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The young women <span class=\"strong\">need instructing</span> on how to dance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Here and there the clothing <span class=\"strong\">requires mending</span> or <span class=\"strong\">cleaning</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They focus on land affairs that <span class=\"strong\">require discussing</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are dances that <span class=\"strong\">need doing</span> and songs that <span class=\"strong\">need singing</span>.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect for Unusual Events: Review", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Present Perfect tense in a variety of ways to connect the past with the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Look at the chart for a review of some ways to use the Present Perfect tense and what kind of words you commonly use with it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Words Commonly Used With It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To talk or ask about events in the recent past, that may still be happening\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">only just <br/>so far<br/> up to now</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Have you only just been told</span> it happens this weekend?<br/> How much <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have you found out so far</span>? <br/> Also because the full moon <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hasn't arrived up to now</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" To talk or ask about experience\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ever</span> (in questions) <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">yet </span>(negatives)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Have you ever wanted</span> to experience the Shimunenga? <br/> The Shimunenga <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hasn't begun yet</span>!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have you</span> recently <span class=\"strong\">arrived</span> in Namwala?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have you</span> ever <span class=\"strong\">wanted</span> to experience the Shimunenga? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have you</span> only just <span class=\"strong\">been told</span> it happens this weekend?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Has</span> the first rain of the season just <span class=\"strong\">fallen</span>? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have you</span> ever <span class=\"strong\">been</span> part of such an exciting event?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How much <span class=\"strong\">have you found</span> out so far? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">haven't been</span> to one myself up to now!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Also because the full moon <span class=\"strong\">hasn't arrived</span> up to now.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Ask family members about cultural activities that they used to participate in or find out about a cultural event at the library.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out where, when and why this event happens in your country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out who usually goes and what they can expect to do there.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put together a poster letting people know about the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the poster to practice talking about the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Bring your poster to class and tell other students about the event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find out about a cultural event in my country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I answer <span class=\"italic\">wh</span>- questions while I find information about the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I put together a poster to tell people about the event. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the poster to tell people in my class about the event.", "type": "text"}]}]}